  </p>

  <div class="chart-container">
    {charts['customer_segments']}
  </div>

  <h3>Customer Segment Analysis</h3>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Segment (by Order Frequency)</th>
        <th class="text-right">Customers</th>
        <th class="text-right">Revenue Share</th>
        <th class="text-right">Total Revenue</th>
        <th class="text-right">Avg Revenue / Customer</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
'''

for seg in data['customer_segments']:
    if seg['customers'] > 0:
        html += f'''      <tr>
        <td>{seg['segment']}</td>
        <td class="text-right">{fmt_number(seg['customers'])}</td>
        <td class="text-right">{seg['revenue_pct']:.1f}%</td>
        <td class="text-right">{fmt_currency(seg['total_revenue'])}</td>
        <td class="text-right">{fmt_currency(seg['avg_revenue_per_customer'])}</td>
      </tr>
'''

html += f'''    </tbody>
  </table>

  <div class="insight-box">
    <strong>Customer Insight:</strong> A majority of customers (58%) make only a single purchase, representing a significant retention opportunity. Customers who return for a second order already match the revenue contribution of one-time buyers (36.6% vs 36.5%). A targeted win-back campaign for one-time buyers and a loyalty incentive for second purchases could materially improve lifetime value.
  </div>

  <div class="insight-box">
    <strong>Note on Demographics:</strong> Customer dimension data (age, gender, loyalty membership status) was not available in the provided dataset. Analysis by demographics and formal loyalty program membership could not be performed. The segmentation above is based solely on transactional order frequency.
  </div>
</div>

<!-- FOOTER -->
<div class="footer">
  <p>Chocolate Retail Sales Performance Report &mdash; Generated from 50,000 transaction records (2023&ndash;2024)</p>
  <p style="margin-top:4px; font-size:0.8rem;">All figures derived directly from data.csv. Dimension tables were not available for brand, category, geographic, or demographic breakdowns.</p>
</div>

</div>
</body>
</html>
'''

# Write final report
with open('output/final_report.html', 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:
    f.write(html)

print("Report written to output/final_report.html")
print(f"Report size: {len(html):,} characters")

